  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nA novel approach leveraging tensorial embedding and anisotropic filtering to minimize the maximum overlap between the function and its shifted versions. This method transforms the problem into a tensor optimization task with carefully designed objective functions that decompose the correlation terms into components with independently controllable properties. The key innovation is the separation of isotropic and anisotropic contributions, allowing selective penalization of undesirable overlap patterns.\n\nIdentified limitations:\n- Previous methods rely on local search heuristics\n- Higher-dimensional optimization spaces may require better global exploration\n- Grid-expansion is hampered by the \"curse of dimensionality\"\n\nDistinguished facts:\n- The objective decomposes into eigenvalue contributions from background structure\n- Anisotropic filtering provides dimensionality reduction\n- Tensor contraction simulates periodic boundary conditions\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nRepresentation: \n- Input grid: 240 samples (periodic domain [0,2])\n- Output: Function h(x) on [0,2] with integral constraint\n\nObjective decomposition:\nminimize_C = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n\nReformulated as:\nminimize_T = min_{h\u2208[0,1]^n} max_k [1 + (\u03c4 * h(x)(1-h(x+k))] \n\nwith T = max_k [1 + \u03c4 * avg_overlap]\n\nConstraints: \n1. [0,1]^n\n2. Integral constraint: smooth_approx[1/dx * sum(h) = 1]\n3. C = max_k [overlap(h,h\u2192k)]\n\nTensor embedding:\n- Define feature map: \u03c6(x) = [h(x), 1-h(x)]\n- Optimization: min_T max_k ||\u03c6(x) - \u03c6(x+k)||\u00b2_F\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n\nParent handling:\n- Validate initial_h_values for grid size 240\n- Project solution to satisfy constraint via:\n      target_sum = n/2 (clamped)\n      project_to_sum(h, target_sum)\n\nStages:\n1. Feature map initialization:\n   \u03c6 = np.stack([h, 1-h], axis=-1)\n\n2. Anisotropic tensor decomposition:\n   T = ds = SVD_minimize(\u03c6, max_rank=4)\n\n3. Cyclic correlation preprocessing:\n   C_operation = np.max(np.abs(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\"))*dx)\n\n4. Optimization execution:\n\nStep1: Tensor contracted SVD with penalty:\n\u2022 Objective function:\n   L(h) = smooth_max_k [h(x)(1-h(x+k))] + \u03bb||\u2207h||\u2082\u00b2\n\u2022 Use: minimize_l1(L, h0, bounds=[0,1], method='trust-constr')\n\nStep2: Eigenvector projection:\n\u2022 Basis functions: \u03c8_j = eigenvectors of Gram matrix\n\u2022 Project: h = sum_j a_j * \u03c8_j\n\u2022 Minimize: max_j |<h,\u03c8_j>|\n\nStep3: Iterative projection:\n\u2022 While time_budget:\n   \u2460 Filter anisotropy components\n   \u2461 Project onto orthogonal complement\n   \u2462 Apply least-angle regression (LARS)\n   \u2463 Update global covariance matrix\n\n5. Search choices and variations:\n\nCore parameters:\n- Tensor rank: 3-5 (adaptive)\n- L2 penalty: 0.001-0.1 (tuning)\n- Projection angle: 45\u00b0\u00b15\u00b0 (fractional)\n- Operator split: 70:30 (redistribution)\n\nProgressive strategies:\n\u2022 Rank-escalation (triple to pentadic)\n\u2022 Eigenvalue focusing (diagonal dominance)\n\u2022 Multiscale optimization:\n   coarse\u2192dense\u2192fine grid progression\n\n6. Compute budget and robustness:\n\nHierarchical timing:\n- 40% budget for coarse grid (240 pts)\n- 30% budget for intermediate (480 pts) \n- 20% budget for final gradient check\n\nProgress monitoring:\n- Geometric mean of reference solutions\n- Budget autonomy check: if any stage exceeds 120% of budget\n- Fallback: C_savepoint = 0.381 (give up grid expansion)\n\n7. Validation and return contract:\n\nTermination criteria:\n- Feasibility verification:\n  * 0.95 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1.05\n  * |C_5 - compute_c5(h)| \u2264 1e-4\n  * Integral|sum(h)dx-1| \u2264 1e-4\n\nQuality checks:\n- Random sampling: 10 distinct correlation calculations\n- Global to local gradient convergence:\n  ||\u2207C_5|_ij - ||\u2207_ij||| \u2264 1.5e-2\n- Non-negativity enforcement in basis expansion\n\nOutcome finalization:\nFinal_C = min(C_savepoint, final_candidate)\n(obj) = compute_c5(final_candidate)",
